Z||000000||Eric||05-05-99||06:31 PM||||Does anyone have any general advice on the 2.8 to 3.1 engine conversion.  <p>I just priced a set of Speed Pro hypereutectic pistons from Summit.  Based on the head volume being 56cc, the compression ratio would be 10.1:1.  Is this to high for the stock computer?  Does anyone know of a particular piston to buy?<p>Auto Zone has a 3.1 crank (981 casting) for about $190.  Could I do better with a used crank?<p>If some of you 3.1 guys are out there, please give me some advice on this undertaking.  Thanks.
Z||000001||speed||05-05-99||06:52 PM||||Eric<br>10.1 is on the high side for street use. Try Federal Mogul that makes piston with a reverse done 0.110" deep for 3.1 blocks and  Silver O Rite makes a piston 0.106" deep (cast pistons) The last one will give you 8.3 to 1 ratio that is good for turbo ( I just bought a set). I had to bought a 3.1 short block from a 95 Lumina(piston are very low 27 cc rev. dome because of the aluminum heads. The 3.1 with iron heads have pistons with less rev. dome.
